lem-bounded-bilateral-sequence-ball-is-c:
## Statement

Let $S$ be a nonempty set, let $\mathcal B(S)$ be the set of bounded functions $S\to\mathbb R$ and let $d_\infty$ be the supremum metric on $\mathcal B(S)$ ([[lem-sup-metric-is-a-metric]]); write $0$ for the zero function. For $R\ge0$ put

$$B_R(S):=\{\,f\in\mathcal B(S)\ :\ |f(s)|\le R\ \text{for every }s\in S\,\}.$$

Let $X_{\pm}$, $\varphi$, $X_2$, $d_2$, $D_\pm$ be as in [[def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space]]. Then:

1. $(\mathcal B(S),d_\infty)$ is a complete metric space ([[def-complete-metric-space]]);
2. for every $R\ge0$, $(B_R(S),d_\infty)$ is a complete metric space;
3. $D_\pm(s,t)=d_2(\varphi(s),\varphi(t))$ is a metric on $X_\pm$ ([[def-metric-space]]), and $\varphi:(X_\pm,D_\pm)\to(X_2,d_2)$ is a bijective isometry ([[def-metric-convergence]] for the underlying notion of distance);
4. consequently $\ell^{\infty}(\mathbb Z)$ with the distance $\|x-y\|_\infty$ is a complete metric space, $B_R$ is complete for every $R\ge0$, and the same holds for the one-sided bounded sequences, that is for $S=\mathbb N$.

thm-henon-coded-invariant-set-is-conjuga:
## Statement

Fix $a\ge100$, let $R=\sqrt a+3$, $L=\sqrt{a-2R}$, let $X_\pm$ and $S_\pm$ be the two-sign bilateral shift space and its shift ([[def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space]]), let $x(s)\in B_R$ be the coded sequence of [[lem-coded-quadratic-recurrence-is-a-contraction]], let

$$F(x,y):=(y,\;y^2-a-x),\qquad h(s):=\bigl(x_{-1}(s),\,x_0(s)\bigr)\qquad(s\in X_\pm),$$

and put $\Lambda:=h(X_\pm)\subseteq\mathbb R^2$. Then:

1. $F\circ h=h\circ S_\pm$, i.e. $F(h(s))=h(S_\pm s)$ for every $s\in X_\pm$, and $\Lambda$ is invariant: $F(\Lambda)=\Lambda$;
2. $h$ is a continuous bijection of $(X_\pm,D_\pm)$ onto $\Lambda$; it is a homeomorphism onto $\Lambda$ with the Euclidean metric ([[def-metric-continuity]]) once the Axiom of Countable Choice is granted, since the proof uses $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$ exactly once, through the equivalence between closed and sequentially closed subsets of $\mathbb R^2$ ([[thm-metric-sequential-closure]]);
3. $\Lambda$ is sequentially compact ([[def-metric-compactness-variants]]) and, granting the Axioms of Countable and Dependent Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-dependent-choice]]), compact ([[def-metric-compactness]]) and a continuous image of the compact space $X_\pm$ ([[thm-continuous-image-of-a-compact-space-is-compact]]);
4. $F|_\Lambda:\Lambda\to\Lambda$ is continuous, topologically mixing, has dense periodic points, and has sensitive dependence on initial conditions with sensitivity constant $2L$; hence $F|_\Lambda$ is chaotic in the stated sense ([[def-cm-topologically-mixing-dense-periodic-and-sensitive-maps]]).

lem-tail-curve-tangents-and-homoclinic-t:
## Statement

Fix $a\ge100$ and let $R=\sqrt a+3$, $L=\sqrt{a-2R}$, $F(x,y)=(y,y^2-a-x)$, $x(s)$, $h$ and the sets $W^s,W^u$ be as in [[def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space]], [[lem-coded-quadratic-recurrence-is-a-contraction]], [[lem-symbol-locality-gives-coding-continuity]] and [[def-stable-unstable-cones-and-line-slopes]]. For $u\in\{-1,+1\}$ put $r_u:=1+u\sqrt{a+1}$ and let

$$M_u^{\sqrt{\ }}(v,w):=u\sqrt{a+v+w}$$

be the square-root update of the coded recurrence. Then:

1. **(hyperbolicity)** the fixed points $(r_u,r_u)$ of $F$ are hyperbolic: $DF(r_u,r_u)$ has two real eigenvalues, one of modulus $>1$ and one of modulus $<1$;
2. **(stable curve at a finite-word point)** let $s\in X_\pm$ be nonconstant with $s_n=u$ for $|n|\ge N$, and put $z_*:=h(s)$. Then there are $\delta_s>0$ and a $C^1$ curve $\gamma_s:(-\delta_s,\delta_s)\to\mathbb R^2$ with $\gamma_s(0)=z_*$, $\gamma_s\bigl((-\delta_s,\delta_s)\bigr)\subseteq W^s(r_u,r_u)$ and tangent $\gamma_s'(0)\in C^s_{1/2}$;
3. **(unstable curve at a finite-word point)** likewise there are $\delta_u>0$ and a $C^1$ curve $\gamma_u:(-\delta_u,\delta_u)\to\mathbb R^2$ with $\gamma_u(0)=z_*$, $\gamma_u\bigl((-\delta_u,\delta_u)\bigr)\subseteq W^u(r_u,r_u)$ and $\gamma_u'(0)\in C^u_{1/2}$; consequently $z_*$ is a transverse homoclinic point of $(r_u,r_u)$ ([[def-stable-unstable-cones-and-line-slopes]]);
4. **(local stable and unstable sets at the fixed point)** put $\rho:=1/8$. Then the set of points $y=(y_{-1},y_0)\in\mathbb R^2$ whose forward orbit stays within Euclidean distance $\rho$ of $(r_u,r_u)$,

$$\Gamma^s_\rho:=\{\,y:\ \bigl\|F^n(y)-(r_u,r_u)\bigr\|_2\le\rho\ \text{for every }n\ge0\,\},$$

is exactly the graph $\{(b,\,r_u+u_0(b)):|b-r_u|\le\rho\}$ of the half-tail solution map $b\mapsto u_0(b)$ obtained from [F2] with the constant reference $y_n:=r_u$ and $b_*:=r_u$; in particular it is a $C^1$ embedded curve through $(r_u,r_u)$ whose tangent at the fixed point lies in $C^s_{1/2}$. With $\Sigma(x,y):=(y,x)$ the same statement holds in the unstable direction: a point has all its backward iterates $F^{-n}(y)$ within distance $\rho$ of $(r_u,r_u)$ if and only if it lies in $\Sigma(\Gamma^s_\rho)$, and $\Sigma(\Gamma^s_\rho)$ is a $C^1$ embedded curve through $(r_u,r_u)$ whose tangent lies in $C^u_{1/2}$.

thm-smooth-fixed-mass-mechanical-horsesh:
## Statement

Grant the Axioms of Countable and Dependent Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-dependent-choice]]), inherited from the compactness and homeomorphism clauses of [[thm-explicit-perturbed-horseshoe-and-transversality]]. Fix $a\ge100$, let $w$, $\beta_\delta$, $P=\pi/2+\delta$ and the stroboscopic map $G_\delta$ be as in [[def-smooth-periodic-oscillator-pulse-model]], and let $X_\pm$, $S_\pm$, $D_\pm$ be the two-sign shift space of [[def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space]]. Then there is $\delta_0>0$, depending only on $a$ and $w$, such that for every $0<\delta<\delta_0$:

1. there is a function $h_\delta:X_\pm\to\mathbb R^2$ that is a homeomorphism of $(X_\pm,D_\pm)$ onto a compact subset $\Lambda_\delta:=h_\delta(X_\pm)$ of $\mathbb R^2$ and satisfies $G_\delta\circ h_\delta=h_\delta\circ S_\pm$; in particular $\Lambda_\delta$ is compact and $G_\delta$-invariant, and $G_\delta|_{\Lambda_\delta}$ is conjugate to the shift;
2. $G_\delta|_{\Lambda_\delta}$ is continuous, topologically mixing, has dense periodic points and is sensitive with a positive constant; hence it is chaotic in the stated sense ([[def-cm-topologically-mixing-dense-periodic-and-sensitive-maps]]);
3. the two constant codes give two hyperbolic fixed points of $G_\delta$, one of each sign;
4. for every nonconstant code $s\in X_\pm$ that is constant outside a finite set, the point $h_\delta(s)$ is a transverse homoclinic point of the corresponding fixed point, and distinct such codes give distinct points ([[def-stable-unstable-cones-and-line-slopes]]).

All statements are about the explicit smooth $P$-periodic ordinary differential equation $q''=-q+\beta_\delta(t)(q^2-a)$ and its time-$P$ map; no empirical claim, measurement or physical assumption occurs.
